body:
Ok thanks for clarification. You can use the hits option.transformData.item: function(item) {} to add any pre-computed data (where you would have done your loop inside) to the item and then access it.

For example:

```js
var hits = instantsearch.widget.hits({
  transformData: {
    item: function(item) {
      item.matchedData = ...
      return item;
    }
  }
});
```

Then in your template, use item.matchedData.

As for helpers, you need to use them like this:

```js
search.templatesConfig.helpers.highlightResults = function (text, render){
  var data = render(text);
  return modifiedData(data)
}
```

To get the actual data object you need to call render on the passed text, this is a bit weird but how hogan.js (our template engine) works with helpers.

